      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "RACI — involvement, over the graph that already exists",
      "prov:value": "The node arrived on the owner's ruling of 2026-09-22 (bean `2xfl`). Until then\nthe definitions below lived here, which made RACI the one methodology in use\nthat the methodology graph could not see. **Read the node first**; everything\nhere assumes it.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 2xfl",
        "2026-09-22"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-22"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/raci/raci.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why an overlay and not a registry",
      "prov:value": "A RACI implemented as its own table of names would be a **second answer to\n\"who is the reviewer\"**, free to disagree with `roles.json` — the drift\nthis repository keeps paying for, most recently in the retired skill\n`roles:` field whose 260 dangling values resolved against nothing\n(`qif9`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean qif9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/raci/raci.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "What this is NOT — the platform's half",
      "prov:value": "**Not permissions.** What an actor may DO is an ODRL rule in `policies/`\n(actions in `skills/permissions/permissions.json`), and cross-cuts roles.\nBeing R for a task says who is expected to do it; performing it also needs a\nrule that permits `perform-task` there (issue #1180).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1180"
      ]
    }
  ]
